Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 14 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 2, row A12): THE PLAN'S ROW FOR THE FINDING G9
 NAMES THE ARC THAT REPLACED ITS FIX

A reader's check of main's answers at Review 80 (agy-002's; row A12, held by main: the row reads so). The
page, the verdict line and the lock of B1878 are mended. The plan's row for the finding G9 still gives the
attribution gate as B1878 landed it, reading the first-parent line, and does not name B1880, which replaced
that reading the same day.

The row's note in the plan's source keeps what it said, and has a dated bracket after it: this is the gate
as B1878 landed it; B1880 replaced that reading the same day; every commit reachable from the tip is read, a
commit that arrives by a merge too. The words are those of B1878's own page and of the plan's own entry for
the re-audit. The page and its data file are built again by the builder.

A test in the plan's lock holds the row: what stood is kept, the bracket names B1880, the page's row carries
both, and B1878's page says the same of itself.

Not said in the bracket, and for the day the fifth series of the enforcement package lands: that series
makes the gate read the author and the committer, the name and the address.

The plan's lock passes: 23 tests. Every gate passes but the count of landings. The row is held by main.
